  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "(a) For arbitrary $n \\geq 2.5$ and $g > 1$, does there exist a knot in $\\mathcal{F}_{n}$ with\ntopological slice genus at least $g$?\n(b) For arbitrary $n \\geq 0$ and $g > 1$, does there exist a knot in $\\mathcal{T}_{n}$ with smooth\nslice genus at least $g$?\n(c) Could the $L^{(2)}$-signature invariants used to obstruct membership in deeper\nlevels of the solvable/bipolar filtration be used to give bounds on the slice\ngenus?",
